# Example Mosquitto ACL for DeskWatch. One login per client, each limited to
# the topics it needs. "deskpanel" is the default topic_prefix.
#
# Topics, from docs/mqtt-schema.md:
#   deskpanel/screen, deskpanel/badges, deskpanel/bridge/status  bridge -> panel
#   deskpanel/panel/status, deskpanel/panel/event                panel -> bridge
#   deskpanel/alert                                              Home Assistant, scripts -> bridge

# The bridge owns everything under deskpanel/ (publishes screens, reads
# button events and alerts).
user deskwatch-bridge
topic readwrite deskpanel/#

# The panel draws what the bridge publishes and reports its own state and
# button presses. It cannot raise alerts or overwrite the screen.
user deskwatch-panel
topic read deskpanel/screen
topic read deskpanel/badges
topic read deskpanel/bridge/status
topic write deskpanel/panel/status
topic write deskpanel/panel/event

# Home Assistant may only raise and clear alerts, so it can never draw on the
# panel directly. HA's own MQTT features (discovery, other devices) use their
# own topics, which belong in the HA rules of your own setup, for example:
#   topic readwrite homeassistant/#
user homeassistant
topic write deskpanel/alert

# A script or cron job that raises alerts (mosquitto_pub) gets the same rule.
# user alert-script
# topic write deskpanel/alert
